 "caption": "Did Vikings wear horned helmets? No. Here are the 3 clues. ⚔️\n\n1. The one almost complete Viking helmet ever found, at Gjermundbu in Norway (1943), is an iron cap with no horns.\n2. Denmark's famous horned helmets from Veksø were made about 900 BC, some 1,500 years before the Viking Age.\n3. The horned look spread after 1876, when Carl Emil Doepler designed the costumes for Wagner's Ring operas at Bayreuth.\n\nWhich myth did you believe the longest? Tell us in the comments and we will check it next. Send this to whoever told you Vikings had horns.\n\nIllustrations: drawn in code by Turns Out. Sources: National Museum of Denmark, Archaeology (AIA), History.com, History Hit.",
